[
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we really want the definition of <code>CochainComplex.of</code> and <code>ChainComplex.of</code> to be <code>def</code>s? Should we change them into <code>abbrev</code>s? I'm asking this because when doing low degree calculations of group/Tate cohomology, we need the fact that <code>(inhomogeneousChains M).X 0</code> is <em>equal</em> to <code>(Fin 0 →G) →₀ M.V</code> reducibly to avoid defEq abuses</p>",
        "id": 591376097,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777381508
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>this appears in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38553\">#38553</a>, maybe <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"459699\">@Joël Riou</span>  you have some suggestions?</p>",
        "id": 591376232,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777381541
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What blocks you from developing some API for <code>inhomogeneousChains</code> so that one can compute with chains directly?</p>",
        "id": 591377232,
        "sender_full_name": "Filippo A. E. Nuccio",
        "timestamp": 1777381748
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I have no opinion about whether <code>ChainComplex.of</code> should be an abbrev or not, but maybe <code>inhomogeneousChains</code> should not be an abbrev, and it would be nice to develop some API for it!</p>",
        "id": 591384629,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777383348
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>[mistaken remark]</p>",
        "id": 591384809,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777383375
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>[more mistaken remark]</p>",
        "id": 591385020,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777383420
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was suggesting making <code>inhomogeneousChains</code> a def instead of an abbrev...</p>",
        "id": 591385276,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777383485
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ah i'm sorry, i was confused</p>",
        "id": 591385453,
        "sender_full_name": "Edward van de Meent",
        "timestamp": 1777383524
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"459699\">Joël Riou</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/changing.20definition.20of.20CochainComplex.2Eof/near/591384629\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I have no opinion about whether <code>ChainComplex.of</code> should be an abbrev or not, but maybe <code>inhomogeneousChains</code> should not be an abbrev, and it would be nice to develop some API for it!</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>but if <code>inhomogeneousChains</code> is a <code>def</code> then what happens if you want to use some lemmas about <code>Finsupp</code> when talking about say <code>(inhomogeneousChains M).X 1</code>?</p>",
        "id": 591423149,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777391743
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Do we copy over all the lemmas about <code>Finsupp</code> on each degree (or in degree 1, 2 and 3?)</p>",
        "id": 591423338,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777391788
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The idea would be to make API which would relate <code>(inhomogeneousChains M).X n</code> and <code>Finsupp</code>: an additive equivalence, and equational lemmas...</p>",
        "id": 591438964,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777395833
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>potentially you're saying we want a wrapper isomorphism between them defined by <code>Iso.refl _</code>?</p>",
        "id": 591439084,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777395876
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I was thinking more of <code>AddEquiv.refl</code> (in terms of unbundled types, rather than as an isomorphism in a category).</p>",
        "id": 591439239,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777395934
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>hmmmm</p>",
        "id": 591650438,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777417055
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I made <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/38661\">#38661</a> as a test and it removed one <code>erw</code>, multiple terminal <code>simp only</code> and some <code>backward.isDefEq</code>s so judging by the result I would say this doesn't look like the wrong thing to do...</p>",
        "id": 591650542,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777417130
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It does not look that the right thing to do either. It seems completely unreasonable to me to have an abbrev for something which contains a term like <code>fun i j =&gt; if h : i = j + 1 then eqToHom (by rw [h]) ≫ d j else 0</code>.</p>",
        "id": 591654529,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777419585
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah I agree the <code>ofHom</code> thing is a bit absurd</p>",
        "id": 591655099,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777419962
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>but my opinion with <code>of</code> stays the same, because that's on types and we probly don't want to change them all the time...</p>",
        "id": 591655152,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777419999
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The  <code>if...</code> is in <code>of</code>, not <code>ofHom</code>...</p>",
        "id": 591656506,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777420812
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>ok... but if we make <code>d</code> a separate def then we don't need to see that? Like what we did in <code>inhomogeneousCochain.d</code> and <code>inhomogeneousCochains</code></p>",
        "id": 591657276,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777421042
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>My point here is just that I think if I construct a cochain complex by <code>of X d ..</code> then when I take <code>(of X d ..).X n</code> it would be good to have  <code>(of X d ..).X n = X n</code> reducibly, or is that a completely crazy idea?</p>",
        "id": 591657901,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777421168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>You certainly need to make a def for the differential.</p>",
        "id": 591660482,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777421581
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah sure I absolutely agree with you on the differentials, but the point I was trying to make is more about <code>X</code>, as that being the main reason of defEq abuses (correct me if I'm wrong here)</p>",
        "id": 591661523,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777421759
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>What I was trying to say is that <code>of</code> could be an abbrev where the <code>d</code> field refers to an auxiliary def.</p>",
        "id": 591663109,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777422007
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think if we do this:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ModuleCat</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eqToHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">blah</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CochainComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">..</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>then lean wouldn't be able to penetrate the definition of <code>d</code> which means we are safe?</p>",
        "id": 591663234,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777422028
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah exactly so we agree :-)</p>",
        "id": 591663328,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777422049
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>This is not what I said.</p>",
        "id": 591664308,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777422814
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are you saying enforcing <code>d</code> as a def into the definition of <code>of</code>? But how do we do that? Or do you mean something else? I'm a bit lost now...</p>",
        "id": 591664426,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777422934
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">refer</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">here</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">an</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">auxiliary</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">shape</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">d_comp_d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">...</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 591664677,
        "sender_full_name": "Joël Riou",
        "timestamp": 1777423079
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>got it, thanks!</p>",
        "id": 591664865,
        "sender_full_name": "Edison Xie",
        "timestamp": 1777423216
    },
    {
        "content": "<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">eqToHom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">h</span><span class=\"o\">])</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- Construct an `α`-indexed chain complex from a dependently-typed differential.</span>\n<span class=\"sd\">-/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sq</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">ChainComplex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">V</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">d</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">X</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">shape</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">d'</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Ne</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">symm</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">w</span><span class=\"o\">)]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">d_comp_d'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">fun</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">i</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">j</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">k</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hjk</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">unfold</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">d'</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">dsimp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">at</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hjk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">substs</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hij</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">hjk</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">only</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">eqToHom_refl</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">id_comp</span><span c